Z||000000||hugh||04-15-2001||07:13 PM||||I took my 1st weekday off in a very long time to go to Ct.for a visit with my youngest sons inlaws.I tuned my wife's van,changed the oil,all filters.Ready to go right?WRONG!!!Just after we got through New York the car lost power.The next 90 miles was a scary ride.I could only accelerate on the downhills and had to stay to the right on the uphills.We were following my son in his 2000 van and almost couldn't keep up.I figured the fuelpump and found a garage in Clinton that would look at it.Saturday they called to say it was the fuelpump and the car was done.They didn't tell me they closed at 12 noon.I got there at about 12:45 and found the doors to there shop locked.That scared the ****  out of me.The gas portion of the place was open,and I got my car.$287.50,it could have been worse.My son was going out on Saturday and had a flat,we took the tire off and found it was no good so we went to a tire store and got a new one.When we got back and put it on,I thought it would be a good idea to check the other front tire and found the same thing.Off to the store again to get the second tire.They only have 23,000 miles on them and look like they had rubbed on something(hopefully warranty will cover them)Bottom line,The weekend cost me and my son almost $500 but we had a good weekend because no one got hurt and I didn't breakdown on the highway.As a side note I saw a late 60's or early 70's Chevy painted bright red with 2 chrome exhaust flaps(like the ones used on tractors only smaller) sticking out the back of the car and they worked,because I could see them move when he stepped on the gas. This should have been in off topic,but no way will I type this again.This was the longest I have been off this forum in almost a year,I guess I am just a Fiero junky!<p>[This message has been edited by hugh (edited 04-15-2001).]||||reg||1
